2026-10-12T09:51:29.7202134Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7212960Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7213736Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7214528Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7214886Z 
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7215186Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7215608Z 
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7216119Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7217217Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7217924Z 
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7218063Z If you would like to
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7218364Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7218539Z 
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7218737Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-12T09:51:29.7219085Z   $ sh ./install-nix
